**1. Task Overview**

The assigned task was to develop a fully responsive, single-page portfolio web application using semantic HTML5 and custom CSS. The key requirements included implementing a fluid layout system using CSS Grid and Flexbox, ensuring responsiveness across all screen widths, and building an interactive mobile navigation menu.

---

**2. Requirements Fulfillment**

All task requirements have been successfully completed:

**Semantic HTML5**
The portfolio is structured using semantic elements including section, nav, footer, header, and main elements to ensure clean, accessible, and meaningful code organization.

**CSS Grid and Flexbox Layouts**
A hybrid layout system was implemented. CSS Grid is used for the services grid, skills groups, education timeline, and contact section. Flexbox is used extensively for navigation, hero stats, project cards, and internal component alignment.

**Responsive Design and Media Queries**
A comprehensive mobile-first responsive design was developed using multiple CSS media query breakpoints at 1024px, 900px, 768px, 760px, 600px, and 480px. The layout adapts seamlessly from desktop (4-column grids) to tablet (2-column grids) to mobile (single-column layouts). All content, typography, and spacing adjust appropriately for each device size.

**Interactive Mobile Navigation**
A custom hamburger menu was built using JavaScript that toggles open and closed, changes the icon between bars and a close symbol, and provides smooth scrolling to sections when links are clicked.

**Additional Interactive Features**
Beyond the core requirements, the portfolio includes a dark and light mode toggle with user preference saved in local storage, a dynamic project carousel with navigation, an accordion-style about section, a live-typing role display, scroll-reveal animations, and a functional contact form integrated with EmailJS.

---

**3. Technology Stack**

The portfolio was built using HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript without any external frameworks. Additional libraries used include Font Awesome for icons and Google Fonts for typography. EmailJS was integrated for contact form functionality.

